# SafeIn5 — Auth API (VS Code "REST Client" extension)
# Install: search "REST Client" (humao.rest-client) in Extensions, then click
# "Send Request" above any request below.
#
# OTP/magic-link codes print to the SERVER LOG (dev mailer), not the response.
# Read the code from the log line: [DEV MAIL] OTP for <email>: NNNNNN
# then set @otp below and Send "Verify OTP".

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@email = sam@example.com
@otp = 942247
@magicToken = nyBcvTe_Pk1b0h5OrC8LKEpVpePrwU6uQSao85cDPOw

### Health — liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Health — readiness (checks DB)
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz

### 1. Register (signup) → 204, OTP printed to server log
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "firstName": "Sam",
  "lastName": "Rivera"
}

### 2. Request OTP (login for an existing account) → 204
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### 3. Verify OTP (set @otp above to the code from the log first)
# @name verifyOtp
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "{{otp}}"
}

### token captured from step 3, reused by the requests below
@token = {{verifyOtp.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4. Get current user (uses the token captured in step 3)
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ── Signals (phase 2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Create a signal (classification: good_practice | be_aware | needs_attention_now)
# @name createSignal
POST {{api}}/signals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "classification": "needs_attention_now",
  "bodyText": "Exposed edge on level 2, no barrier"
}

### Create an ANONYMOUS signal (author hidden in every read path)
POST {{api}}/signals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "classification": "be_aware",
  "bodyText": "Someone bypassing the lockout",
  "anonymous": true
}

### Feed — all signals, newest first
GET {{api}}/feed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Feed — with limit
GET {{api}}/feed?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### My signals
GET {{api}}/signals/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one signal by id (uses the id from Create Signal)
GET {{api}}/signals/{{createSignal.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ── Supervisor loop (phase 3) ────────────────────────────────────────
# First make a supervisor (role is on the tenant membership), then log THAT
# user in (steps 1-3) so {{token}} has role=supervisor:
#   UPDATE user_tenant_membership m SET role='supervisor'
#     FROM app_user u WHERE u.id=m.user_id AND u.email='boss@example.com';

### Acknowledge (supervisor only) → 200, or 403 for a worker
POST {{api}}/signals/{{createSignal.response.body.$.id}}/acknowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Close (supervisor only, note required) → 200
POST {{api}}/signals/{{createSignal.response.body.$.id}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "closeNote": "Barrier reinstated, area cleared" }

### Feed — only open signals (supervisor "needs response")
GET {{api}}/feed?status=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Negative — create without token → 401
POST {{api}}/signals
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classification": "be_aware", "bodyText": "x" }

### Negative — bad classification → 400
POST {{api}}/signals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "classification": "stop_now", "bodyText": "x" }

### 5. Request magic link → 204, link printed to server log
POST {{api}}/auth/magic-link
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### 6. Verify magic link (set @magicToken above to the token in the logged URL)
# @name verifyMagic
GET {{api}}/auth/magic/{{magicToken}}

### 7. Get current user via magic-link token
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{verifyMagic.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 8. Refresh (needs the refresh cookie set at login)
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh

### 9. Logout → 204
POST {{api}}/auth/logout

### Negative — wrong OTP → 401
POST {{api}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "code": "000000"
}

### Negative — invalid email → 400
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

# ── Video upload (chunked, DIRECT-TO-S3) ─────────────────────────────
# Single endpoint POST /uploads/next drives a lockstep S3 multipart upload (see
# docs/md/BACKEND_UPLOAD_SPEC.md). Auth is OPTIONAL — uncomment Authorization to
# tie the upload to your account; leave it off for an anonymous upload.
#
# IMPORTANT: the chunk BYTES go DIRECTLY to S3 via the presigned `url` in each
# response — NOT through this API — and you must read the ETag from that S3 PUT
# and echo it back. REST Client can't do the S3 PUT or read the ETag, so the V*
# calls below are illustrative (paste real ETags); the negative cases are fully
# runnable. Use the frontend (or the scripted E2E) for a real end-to-end run.

### V1. Start an upload (no sessionId) -> { sessionId, status:"in_progress", nextChunkNumber:1, url }
# @name uploadStart
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "clip.mp4",
  "mime": "video/mp4",
  "size": 6291456,
  "chunkSize": 5242880,
  "chunkCount": 2
}

### (out of band) PUT the chunk-1 bytes to uploadStart's `url` directly to S3,
### then read the ETag response header. eTag must be a JSON string INCLUDING the
### quotes S3 returns, e.g. "\"d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e\"".
@sessionId = {{uploadStart.response.body.$.sessionId}}

### V2. Confirm chunk 1 -> { nextChunkNumber:2, url } (paste the real chunk-1 ETag)
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}", "chunkNumber": 1, "eTag": "\"PASTE_CHUNK1_ETAG\"" }

### V3. Resume — chunkNumber:0 re-issues the URL for the chunk still awaited
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}", "chunkNumber": 0 }

### V4. Confirm the LAST chunk (chunkNumber === chunkCount) -> { status:"completed", videoId }
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}", "chunkNumber": 2, "eTag": "\"PASTE_CHUNK2_ETAG\"" }

### Negative — unknown session → 410 { code:"EXPIRED_SESSION" }
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sessionId": "sess_nope", "chunkNumber": 1, "eTag": "\"x\"" }

### Negative — unsupported mime → 422 { code:"UNSUPPORTED_MIME" }
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
Content-Type: application/json

{ "filename": "a.txt", "mime": "text/plain", "size": 100, "chunkSize": 100, "chunkCount": 1 }

### Negative — inconsistent chunk plan → 422 { code:"INVALID_CHUNK_PLAN" }
POST {{api}}/uploads/next
Content-Type: application/json

{ "filename": "a.mp4", "mime": "video/mp4", "size": 100, "chunkSize": 50, "chunkCount": 5 }
